rachel_mktg: Heads-up: Received multiple SDR complaints that some inbound EU leads were routed to the US pool this morning between 08:05-08:10. Saw ~12 leads.
deepak_revops: I pulled the webhook logs — HubSpot sometimes emits property updates in two separate webhook events: one with email/phone and later one with geo/territory. If our RR triggers on the first event we assign prematurely.
vera_salesops: That matches the symptoms. Also noticed several leads have \"pending\" in HS for ~700ms before territory is set.
noah_eng: We currently treat any new contact creation webhook as an assign event. We need a guard: only assign when territory is present OR when a pending_assignment flag is set to false.
rana_sdrlead: Quick ask: can we avoid buffering more than 1s? SDRs expect <2s for routing.
deepak_revops: Proposal: add a 750ms soft-debounce at the router plus an idempotent assign_token derived from external_id+event_id so later webhook won't duplicate. Also add an immediate fallback that infers territory by IP when missing but mark as "inferred" so SDRs can filter.
noah_eng: Implementation sketch: add pending_assignment property on the HS contact, initial value true; router only assigns once pending_assignment=false OR territory!=null. Webhook handler sets pending_assignment=false when territory is received or after timeout.
rachel_mktg: How do we set that flag from HS? Can we do it via workflow action?
deepak_revops: Yes: HubSpot workflow can set a custom property pending_assignment (boolean). Add a workflow step after enrichment to set it false. For early exit we run a timed escalation that sets it false after 750ms.
noah_eng: Pseudocode for router logic:
```js
// router handler
const payload = req.body; // HS webhook
const token = `${payload.externalId}:${payload.hsEventId}`;
if (hasAssigned(token)) return; // idempotent
if (!payload.properties.territory && !payload.properties.pending_assignment_false) {
  if (inferenceEnabled) {
    payload.properties.territory = inferTerritory(payload.ip);
    payload.properties.territory_inferred = true;
  } else {
    // delay short window
    scheduleRetry(token, 750);
    return;
  }
}
assignLeadToBucket(payload, token);
```
vera_salesops: We should also add a HubSpot workflow toggle to temporarily delay assignment by 1s for any contact created via webform POSTs while we test. That is reversible.
rachel_mktg: Is there a simpler mitigation we can flip now?
ana_sdrlead: (typo, ana_sdrlead) Suggestion: Have marketing enable a hidden form field territory_hint populated by form JS. That reduces dependency on IP inference for some geos.
deepak_revops: Good idea for long term. For now: Plan = 1) deploy router idempotency + 750ms soft-debounce; 2) create HS workflow to set pending_assignment=false after enrichment; 3) flip temporary HS toggle to delay assignment by 1s for inbound forms; 4) add metric lead.assign_duplicate_count and territory_inferred_rate.
noah_eng: I'll push a small canary for the router change (feature flag: router.pending_guard). Can we schedule canary at 11:00 UTC?
rachel_mktg: 11:00 works. I'll notify SDR leads.
hs-bot: hubspot-bot: Workflow updated: inbound-enrich -> set pending_assignment=false (workflow id: wf_8842).
deepak_revops: Quick rollback plan: if overflow_pool > 40 in 10m or assign_duplicate_count spikes >5/min revert feature flag.
noah_eng: Canary deploy kicked off by deploy-bot at 2024-12-03T11:00:12Z (build 2024.12.03.101).
deepak_revops: Early canary metrics: assign_duplicate_count down from 3/min -> 0.4/min; territory_inferred_rate stable at 2.1%.
rana_sdrlead: Seeing fewer misroutes in the SDR queue, will monitor in next 30m and report.
rachel_mktg: Great. After 24h we'll evaluate if the HS workflow can be removed or reduced. Add a retrospective note to marketing playbook.
vera_salesops: Also add a short entry to SDR playbook: how to handle 'territory_inferred' leads (prefilter/flag).
noah_eng: I'll open PR and runbook: PR #1324 + runbook link (will paste when ready).
rachel_mktg: Thanks everyone :sparkles: Closing thread once metrics stable +24h.
